cheremsha.hop:
Use case: stylized-concept.
Asset type: 16-frame sprite sheet of a single complete RABBIT HOP, transparent RGBA.
Reference image 1 defines Cheremsha's exact identity: a compact fantastical HARE + LION hybrid, huge long broad rabbit ears, serious gentle lion muzzle, thick shaggy tawny-grey mane, round fluffy short body and strong short hind legs. Reference image 2 defines only the realistic fur rendering and recognizable side-profile face from the existing walk test. Preserve this hybrid identity; not a normal lynx.
PRIMARY CHANGE: she now HOPS LIKE A RABBIT instead of walking. The two hind legs act TOGETHER, pushing off simultaneously and tucking forward together. The forepaws reach ahead together for landing, absorb impact first, then the hind paws recover under the body. No alternating walking, no one-legged hopping, no permanently trailing leg.
Produce exactly SIXTEEN distinct sequential poses, uniform 4-column by 4-row square grid, total canvas SQUARE. Right-facing SIDE PROFILE. One complete hop cycle, not sixteen separate hops. Same character, same fur, head proportions, scale and camera every cell. Far paws can be slightly darker but there are exactly four anatomical legs.
Frames:
1 calm ready stance;
2 begin crouch, bend both rear hocks and both forelegs;
3 deepest compact crouch, hindquarters coil, paws close under body;
4 hind legs extend together for push-off, forepaws lift;
5 toe-off, both hind legs finish extending behind, forepaws fold;
6 early flight, both hind paws begin recovering forward;
7 mid-flight, all four paws tucked;
8 compact apex pose, hind paws fully tucked, forepaws beginning to reach;
9 late flight, forepaws reach forward together, hind paws remain tucked;
10 forepaws extend down in preparation for landing;
11 both forepaws touch down, hindquarters still raised;
12 forelegs flex to absorb landing, both hind paws swing forward under belly;
13 hind paws touch down together under body;
14 settle with a small body compression;
15 rise gently back to ready stance;
16 nearly ready, leads smoothly into frame 1.
IN-PLACE REGISTRATION: Do NOT draw a large vertical airborne jump arc inside the cells; the app adds the physical arc and screen travel. Keep the torso centered around the SAME position in all sixteen cells, except small crouch/landing compression. Maintain a constant virtual ground baseline at 90% cell height for contact poses. Flight poses have tucked feet above this baseline. Ears and every paw stay inside the cell, at least 8% padding. Body fills about 78% of each cell. Small natural ear lag is allowed, no identity/face morphing.
High-quality realistic softly painted fur matching the references. Actual alpha-zero transparent empty background, no white matte, checkerboard, shadow, floor, text, labels, numbers, scenery or props. Clean fur edges without colored residue.

